# Gameplay reproduction for inc-fdi2: does casting the priest spell
# "Blasphemy" (lib/pspells.irh ~5924) actually charge the two fatigue points
# its own Desc promises? On master the EV_EFFECT handler that would charge
# them was missing; the worktree branch adds
#   if (!EActor->LoseFatigue(2,true)) return ABORT;
#   return NOTHING;
# Sibling of tools/keys/bestow-curse-menu-ability.keys; see that file's
# header for the wizard-mode setup this one repeats.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/blasphemy-fatigue-play.keys 1
#
# Wizard mode sets up the scenario: a priest, Infinite Mana and Freeze
# Monsters (Wizard Mode Switches rows 8 and 11) so the mana check on
# Creature::Invoke (a belt-and-braces measure -- SP_KNOWN|SP_INNATE from
# Learn Any Spell already skips that check, src/Magic.cpp:4950) and the
# summoned target's own turn never interfere, and Learn Any Spell for
# Blasphemy (SP_KNOWN|SP_PRIMAL|SP_INNATE, src/Debug.cpp:862) so a level-1
# priest can cast a 7th-level, 32-mana spell at all -- this routes the cast
# through Creature::Invoke and EV_INVOKE (Player.cpp:862), not Creature::Cast,
# since SP_INNATE is set; EV_INVOKE still ReThrows EV_EFFECT
# (src/Magic.cpp:5003), which is the event this bead's fix hangs off.
#
# The target is a plain "human" (MA_HUMAN, no M_EVIL/M_GOOD/M_LAWFUL/
# M_CHAOTIC flags in lib/mon2.irh:444) so it is a true-neutral sapient
# creature Blasphemy actually affects (Evil creatures, like the goblin the
# sibling scripts use, are immune by the spell's own rule; good and neutral
# outsiders/creatures are not).
#
# The caster's CURRENT fatigue is read off the status line at the bottom of
# the play screen ("FP:x/5") on the human-summoned and cast-blasphemy dumps --
# the character sheet's own "Fatigue Points" row (src/Sheet.cpp:322) is the
# character's MAXIMUM fatigue, which this cast does not change, so the 'd'
# sheet dumps below are read for confirmation only, not for the delta.

@include chargen-priest.keys
ESC

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*7
SPACE
DOWN*3
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Blasphemy"
ENTER

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Humans"
@choose "human"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:human-summoned

w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
RIGHT
@dump:human-before
ESC

d
@dump:fatigue-before
ESC

m
@choose "Blasphemy"
RIGHT
ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:cast-blasphemy

d
@dump:fatigue-after
ESC

w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
RIGHT
@dump:human-after
ESC

v
@dump:message-log
@while "Messages" ESC

@quit
